  "_comment": [
    "Seed scenario for the Square unit. Fork-owned data, not code.",
    "Ids and example values are taken from Square's own documentation examples",
    "so that a consumer reading the docs recognises what comes back:",
    "  merchant/location/order  https://developer.squareup.com/reference/square/locations-api/list-locations",
    "  catalog ITEM + variation https://developer.squareup.com/reference/square/catalog-api/retrieve-catalog-object",
    "  order id shape           https://developer.squareup.com/reference/square/orders-api/create-order",
    "  tender id + shape        https://developer.squareup.com/reference/square/orders-api/pay-order",
    "The COMPLETED order carries closed_at and a tender that covers its whole",
    "total, because Square cannot produce one that does not: COMPLETED means",
    "'Completed orders are fully paid. This is a terminal state.'",
    "  https://developer.squareup.com/reference/square/enums/OrderState",
    "  https://developer.squareup.com/reference/square/objects/Order",
    "Timestamps are fixed so that SearchOrders date filtering is reproducible.",
    "Keys are snake_case throughout, which is the one departure from the",
    "TypeScript reference's copy of this file: every other JSON this project",
    "publishes or accepts -- profiles, the control plane, the wire projections --",
    "is snake_case, and a camelCase seed document would be the only exception."
  ],
